A [[farm]]ing<ref name="Topps">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Finest Star Wars|subset=Tales of the Jedi|cardname=Inquisitor|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/394545/cid/23204404}}</ref> '''village''' was where [[Ahsoka Tano]] was in hiding. A [[Unidentified village sister|village sister]], [[Unidentified village brother|village brother]], and [[Unidentified old man (Ahsoka Tano)|old man]] were among its inhabitants. After it was revealed to the brother that a [[Jedi]] was residing in the village, he alerted the [[Galactic Empire]] of such. The Empire sent the [[Eleventh Brother]], who burned the village and killed most, leaving only the old man and brother alive.<ref name="Resolve">{{TOTJ|Resolve (episode)}}</ref>

==History==
On a sunny day in the village, bales of harvested crops fell on a [[Unidentified village sister|girl living there]], but [[Ahsoka Tano]], who was in hiding under the alias Ashla, saved her using [[the Force]]. The Villager's [[Unidentified village brother|brother]] overheard that "Ashla" was a Jedi, and as a supporter of the new [[Galactic Empire]], he alerted them. While the two women were gone to [[Mon-Hella]], the [[Eleventh Brother]] arrived at the village. Eleventh Brother, thinking he had been lied to, burned the village and killed most of its inhabitants, apart from the [[Unidentified old man (Ahsoka Tano)|Old Man]] and the brother, who heavily regretted his actions at this stage. Tano arrived back at the burning village, and the Inquisitor, who relished his prestigious find, raised his lightsaber to murder her. Ahsoka thought quickly, and used a quick but deadly move that ended the Inquisitor. She freed the trapped two and left the village with the survivors.<ref name="Resolve" />

